# DynamoDB + ElectroDB

## Mandatory

- Persist all domain data in **DynamoDB**.
- Interact with DynamoDB **only via ElectroDB** (`Entity` / `Service`). Do not call raw `GetItem`/`Query`/`PutItem` from use-cases; keep Document Client inside the ElectroDB adapter wiring.
- Prefer **single-table** design with clear PK/SK and GSIs per access pattern.

## Adapter boundary

```
ports/     → ProductRepository, TransactionRepository, …
adapters/outbound/dynamodb/ → ElectroDB entities + repository implementations
```

- Use-cases depend on repository **ports**, never on ElectroDB types.
- Map ElectroDB records ↔ domain entities inside the adapter.

## Entities to cover

Products (stock), customers, deliveries, transactions — aligned with API domains.

## Seed & local

- Idempotent seed script for dummy products (no create-product HTTP endpoint).
- Document table name(s), indexes, and env (`AWS_REGION`, table name, credentials/profile).
- Tests: mock repository ports; optionally integration-test ElectroDB against local/dev table.

## Anti-patterns

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — ORM/SQL or raw SDK in use-case
await prisma.product.update(...)
await dynamo.send(new UpdateItemCommand(...))

// ✅ GOOD — ElectroDB behind a port
await productRepo.decrementStock({ productId, qty: 1 })
```
